The '''Toyota Camry (XV70)''' is a [[mid-size car]] produced by [[Toyota]] from June 2017 to October 2024. Replacing the [[Toyota Camry (XV50)|XV50]] series, the XV70 represented the eighth generation of the [[Toyota Camry]] in all markets outside Japan,<ref name="Wheels">{{cite news |last1=Mathioudakis |first1=Byron |title=2017 Detroit Motor Show: 2018 Toyota Camry revealed |url=https://www.wheelsmag.com.au/news/events/1701/2017-detroit-motor-show-all-new-2018-toyota-camry-revealed |work=[[Wheels (magazine)|Wheels]] |location=Australia |date=10 January 2017 |access-date=23 January 2017}}</ref> which followed a different generational lineage. The XV70 Camry was introduced at the [[North American International Auto Show#2017|2017 North American International Auto Show]],<ref name=ConsumerReports/> it is built on the [[Toyota TNGA-K platform|GA-K]] platform.<ref name="usnews"/>


